## NOTES

UPCASTING: only `tg_line`, `tg_ring`, and `tg_poly` can upcast to tg_geom.

## vendored tg patches

Local fixes on top of tg v0.4.0 live as one patch file per fix in
`vendor/tg/patches/`; `vendor/tg/update.ts` re-applies them automatically
after fetching a fresh amalgamation. Each patch has its full story in its
header, uses tg-repo-relative paths (so it can become an upstream PR
as-is), and should be dropped once a tg release includes the fix:

1. `0001-writers-dispatch-on-base-*`: recursive geojson/wkt/wkb writers
   segfault on upcast collection children (committed back in 2024 as
   34bc35d, now carried as a patch).
2. `0002-parse_wkb_posns-*`: uint32 overflow in the WKB point-count bounds
   check → out-of-bounds read from a crafted blob.
3. `0003-parse_wkb-multi-*`: multiline/multipolygon parsers store NULL
   child members from corrupted WKB → NULL deref in consumers.

0002 and 0003 were found by the WKB corruption fuzzer in
`tests/test-memory.c`; both are reachable from any WKB entry point
(`tg_to_wkt(<blob>)`, `tg_geom(<blob>)`, tg0 `_shape` inserts).

## geom idx

```sql
select
  tg_intersect(
    tg_geom(:big_blob, 'ystripes'),
    tg_point(latitude, longitude)
  )
from businesses;
```

tg0 v2 covers the indexed-parse idea: geometry columns take
`indexing=none|natural|ystripes`, and stored candidates are parsed with that
index at query time (`tg_parse_wkb_ix`).

- [x] `tg_group_bbox()`
- [x] distance stuff -- `tg_distance_sphere(point, geom)` (great-circle
      meters; the knn workstream's distance kernel). Planar measurements
      still deliberately unwrapped
- [x] KNN support -- `geomcol match <point> order by distance limit n` on
      tg0 tables (knn workstream): best-first walk of the column's rtree
      node blobs, `metric=geodesic|planar` per geometry column, same-column
      predicate + `distance <= r` folded into the walk
- [ ] extensions

## constructors

- [x] `tg_point()` -- 3/4-arg Z/ZM arities added (ticket 12); M-only construction intentionally unsupported
- [.] `tg_multipoint(p1, p2, ...)`
- [.] `tg_group_multipoint(p)`
- [x] `tg_geometrycollection(g1, g2)`
- [x] `tg_group_geometrycollection(g)` -- registered as the primary name; `tg_group_geometry_collection` (underscored) kept as a deprecated alias, same step/final pair (ticket 08)
- [x] `tg_linestring(p1, p2, ...)` (alias to `tg_line`)
- [x] `tg_group_line(p)` -- registered as `tg_group_line` (matching `tg_line`, not `tg_linestring`); no `_linestring`-spelled alias shipped
- [x] `tg_ring(p1, p2, ...)`
- [x] `tg_group_ring(p)`
- [x] `tg_polygon(exterior, hole1, hole2, ...)` (params are rings)
- [x] `tg_group_polygon(ring)` -- shipped the 1-arg form: first row is the exterior, subsequent rows are holes (the 2-arg exterior+holes sketch below was deferred, see 07-group-line-ring-polygon.md)
- [x] `tg_multilinestring(l1, l2, ...)`
- [ ] `tg_group_multilinestring(l1, l2, ...)`
- [x] `tg_multipolygon(p1, p2)`
- [ ] `tg_group_multipolygon(p)`

- [x] `tg_rect(minX, minY, maxX, maxY)` / `tg_rect(minP, maxP)` -- represented at the SQL boundary as the equivalent closed-ring Polygon (ticket 11, option a); no dedicated pointer subtype
- [x] `tg_segment(aX, aY, bX, bY)` / `tg_segment(aP, bP)` -- represented at the SQL boundary as the equivalent 2-point LineString (ticket 11, option a); no dedicated pointer subtype

